  "scientific_conclusions": {
    "terminology_standard": "optical_reference_agreement (NOT ground_truth_accuracy)",
    "june_baseline_summary": "Under primary strict validation (SCL 6 Water vs SCL 5 Bare Ground), the June 10 SAR candidate water mask achieves an optical-reference agreement Precision of 0.5910, Recall of 0.5141, and F1 of 0.5499 over 541,242 evaluated cells (53.59% of the study AOI). The 3-day temporal gap captures pre-monsoon river discharge changes along dynamic braided bars.",
    "july_flood_summary": "In the peak flood epoch, heavy monsoon convective cloud cover leaves only 11.83% of the study AOI (119,478 cells) evaluable under strict criteria. Within this cloud-free spatial domain, SAR exhibits a high detection sensitivity (Recall = 0.7817, F1 = 0.6010, IoU = 0.4296). However, because the evaluable pixels are strongly spatially clustered in cloud gaps, July is formally designated as PARTIALLY_EVALUABLE and must not be extrapolated as a full-scene accuracy rating."
